    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Isolated per-change commit with az evidence" location="plan.md § High-Risk Items">One GUID = one commit. Message body quotes the `az ad sp show --id ... --query "appRoles[?value=='{roleName}'] | [0]"` invocation + result GUID; this is the audit trail for T3 later.</pattern>
      <pattern name="ADR-028 MI-Dataverse-App-User" location=".claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md">Graph app-role grants are ceremony-critical; wrong GUID silently 403s app-only calls. GraphAppRoles.cs is the r3-landed compile-time constant that H10 (Wave C4) will iterate.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Emit the 🔒 RIGOR LEVEL block (FULL). Load bff-extensions.md + ADR-028 + auth.md + patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md + notes/r3-handoff.md.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Baseline">Read GraphAppRoles.cs; enumerate the 11 null AppRoleId slots (verify count per discovery report §12: FileStorageContainerSelected, FilesReadAll, FilesReadWriteAll, SitesReadAll, SitesReadWriteAll, UserReadAll, GroupReadAll, MailRead, MailReadWrite, MailSend, MailboxSettingsRead); capture the exact role-name string for each.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Verify az auth">Run `az account show` to confirm operator's own AAD identity is authenticated (NOT a service principal, per spec.md NFR-11 auditability).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Enumerate Graph SP">Run `az ad sp show --id 00000003-0000-0000-c000-000000000000 --query "appRoles[]" -o json` and save output to a scratchpad file for evidence.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Enumerate Dynamics SP (if any)">If any of the 10 null roles are Dynamics roles (not Graph), run `az ad sp show --id 00000007-0000-0000-c000-000000000000 --query "appRoles[]" -o json` similarly.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Per-GUID commit loop">For each of the 11 null roles: (a) locate matching role in az output by role-name; (b) extract exact GUID; (c) populate GraphAppRoles.cs; (d) `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` to verify no new warnings; (e) commit with message quoting the az invocation + result line. Repeat 11 times.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Verify build">Full `dotnet build` on Sprk.Bff.Api succeeds with zero new warnings (net10 analyzers-as-errors).</step>
    <step order="7" name="Publish-size report">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/` per CLAUDE.md §10 bullet 4. Measure compressed size; report absolute + delta vs 44.96 MB net10 baseline in PR description scratch.</step>
    <step order="8" name="CVE scan">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` per NFR-02; report zero HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Index update">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 005 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Deviations">Document any deviation (e.g., role-name not found in az output — see escalation) in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If az enumeration returns unexpected/missing role IDs (any of the 10 role names does not match an appRole in the Graph OR Dynamics SP catalog), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than filling a Guess-GUID. Silent wrong GUID is the exact T3 silent-failure mode this task exists to prevent (per plan.md § High-Risk Items + spec.md § Human Escalation Triggers for CLAUDE.md project row).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="az">Azure CLI for `ad sp show` enumeration</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build + publish + vulnerability scan</tool>
    <tool name="git">Per-GUID isolated commits</tool>
  </tools>

