  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given GraphAppRoles.cs, when scanning all 14 AppRoleId slots, then all are populated with valid GUIDs (no `null` values remain).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `git log --oneline src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/GraphAppRoles.cs`, when counting commits in this task's PR, then exactly 11 commits populate GUIDs (one per GUID); +1 doc-reconciliation commit updating spec.md/design.md/CLAUDE.md "10 of 14" → "11 of 14".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given each populated GUID's commit message, when reading, then it quotes the exact `az ad sp show --id ...` invocation + the response line naming the role.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`, when running, then build succeeds with zero new warnings (net10 analyzers-as-errors).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`, when measuring compressed output, then publish size ≤ 60 MB AND delta vs 44.96 MB baseline is reported in PR description (per NFR-01).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`, when running, then zero HIGH-severity CVEs (per NFR-02).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no other file in src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is modified (git diff scope = 1 file).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: if any GUID could not be resolved from az output, the escalation trigger fired (BLOCKED.md exists) — the task did NOT proceed with a guess.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-13 H10 escalation gate + Phase A owner directive. Wrong GUID silently fails T3 in H10 (Wave C4) → app-only Graph 403s in production. Feeds Phase B task 015 (Grant-GraphAppRoles.ps1 helper) and Wave C4 H10 handler.</notes>

